node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Nothing here reads a .env today, but this project documents CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and GH tokens, so one is a
# plausible future addition — and it would otherwise be committed in silence.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output, caches and editor state. None exist today; all are cheap to exclude before they do.
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.wrangler/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Heap snapshots from `npm run probe`. A snapshot is a dump of everything the process held — process.env
# included — so these must never be committed, and are worth deleting once a leak hunt is over.
.probe/
*.heapsnapshot

# The private record of what actually broke, with the real hostnames and repo names behind the generic ones
# used in the source. Deliberately not published; back it up separately, since it does not survive a clone.
INCIDENTS.md

# The scrub script holds the same mapping — every real name beside its replacement — so publishing it would
# undo the scrub it performs. It is only useful to someone who already has the private mapping anyway.
scripts/scrub.mjs

# The demo workspace: invented repositories, rebuilt on demand by `npm run demo`.
.demo/
